What is the difference between a while loop and a do...while loop?
A while loop checks the condition first, so the loop may execute zero times if the condition is false. 
A do...while loop executes the code first and checks the condition afterward, so it always executes at least once.

What is the difference between: for and while?
Both for and while loops are used to repeat code.
A for loop puts initialization, condition, and update together in the loop statement, while 
A while loop mainly contains the condition, with initialization and update usually written separately.

What is the difference between break and continue in JavaScript?
Break : stop the loop and terminate the excuteing loop
Continue: stop or skip the current iteration and move to next iteration

What is an infinite loop? And give me one example of how an infinite loop can happen in JavaScript?
An infinite loop is a loop that never terminates because its condition always remains true or the loop variable is not updated correctly.

Ex: let i = 1;
while( i < 10){
    console.log(i)
}

What is a nested loop? And explain what happens when an inner loop is inside an outer loop?
A loop containing another loop is called a nested loop.
A nested loop is a loop inside another loop. For every one iteration of the outer loop, the inner loop completes all of its iterations.

What is the difference between: for...in, for...of
for...in iterates over the keys of an object and indexes of an array, while for...of iterates directly over the values of an iterable such as an array or string.

